  "reading_the_numbers": [
    "density is the share of every possible two- or three-knot reading that the scoring rule accepts as a word; it is the hit rate a mapping gets for free.",
    "order_shuffle scrambles the knots within each cord; khipu_shuffle deals each khipu's knots back out to its cords at random. The mapping is held fixed.",
    "refit searches for the best one-to-one mapping on the real cords and again on scrambled cords, so a fitted score is compared with fitted scores.",
    "p_upper cannot go below 1/(trials+1). A hit means a string is in a word list. It does not mean the cord says that word."
  ],
